Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:3px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6B6460;margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.6\">Lens guide</p><p style=\"text-align:center;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:26px;line-height:1.15;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">What to choose</p>","display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"block_padding_top":0,"block_padding_right":0,"block_padding_bottom":0,"block_padding_left":0}}},{"content_type":"block","type":"text","data":{"content":"<table width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;background:#3B2C27;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;color:#FAF9F6\">LENS</td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;background:#3B2C27;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;color:#FAF9F6\">WHAT IT&#39;S FOR</td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;background:#3B2C27;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;color:#FAF9F6\">FROM</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\"><b>Single vision</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\">One prescription across the whole lens, for distance or reading</td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\">$140</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\"><b>Progressive</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\">Near and far in one lens, with a smooth change in between</td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\">$240</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\"><b>Non-prescription</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\">Blue light or a custom tint, no correction</td><td style=\"padding:10px 6px;word-break:normal;overflow-wrap:normal;border-bottom:1px solid #DFD1C0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4\">$140</td></tr></table>","display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"block_padding_top":4,"block_padding_right":0,"block_padding_bottom":20,"block_padding_left":0}}},{"content_type":"block","type":"text","data":{"content":"<p style=\"text-align:left;color:#1E1512;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px\"><b>Materials:</b> CR39 for everyday wear, Polycarbonate for strength (shatter resistant), Trivex for feather-light comfort, and High Index 1.67 for strong prescriptions. <b>Anti-reflective coating is included on every lens.</b></p>","display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"block_padding_top":0,"block_padding_right":0,"block_padding_bottom":0,"block_padding_left":0}}}]}]}]},{"content_type":"section","type":"section","data":{"properties":{},"display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"background_color":"#FAF9F6","inner_padding_top":24,"inner_padding_right":24,"inner_padding_bottom":8,"inner_padding_left":24,"stack_on_mobile":true}},"rows":[{"data":{"styles":{"column_layout":"1-column-full-width"}},"columns":[{"blocks":[{"content_type":"block","type":"text","data":{"content":"<p style=\"text-align:center;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:3px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6B6460;margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.6\">Your questions</p><p style=\"text-align:center;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:26px;line-height:1.15;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">Prescription FAQ</p>","display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"block_padding_top":0,"block_padding_right":0,"block_padding_bottom":0,"block_padding_left":0}}},{"content_type":"block","type":"text","data":{"content":"<p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">What prescriptions can you make?</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 24px\">Single vision, readers and progressive. Looking for something truly custom? Reply and tell us, and we&#39;ll work on it with you.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">Do I need my PD?</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 24px\">Yes. It&#39;s usually on your prescription. If it isn&#39;t, ask your optometrist, or use the virtual try-on on our product pages, which can measure it for you.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">How long does it take?</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 24px\">Your order ships in 3&ndash;4 business days once we&#39;ve checked your prescription. Complex prescriptions and custom orders can take up to three weeks. We&#39;ll email you if yours will.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">Can I change my order after I place it?</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 24px\">Not once it&#39;s placed. Your lenses go straight into production with our lab, so double-check your prescription before you check out.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">Can I return or exchange prescription lenses?</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 24px\">Prescription (RX) orders are final sale, because your lenses are made just for you. If your order arrives damaged, defective or wrong, email <a href=\"mailto:customer@solkyst.ca\" style=\"color:#3B2C27\">customer@solkyst.ca</a> within 48 hours of delivery with your order number and photos, and we&#39;ll work with you on it.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-style:italic;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 6px\">Can my own optometrist fit lenses in your frames?</p><p style=\"text-align:left;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#1E1512;margin:0 0 24px\">Our frames are Rx-able, so yes. Just ask your optometrist to confirm they&#39;ll work with your prescription.</p>","display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"block_padding_top":0,"block_padding_right":0,"block_padding_bottom":0,"block_padding_left":0}}}]}]}]},{"content_type":"section","type":"section","data":{"properties":{},"display_options":{"show_on":"all"},"styles":{"background_color":"#F4EEE8","inner_padding_top":40,"inner_padding_right":24,"inner_padding_bottom":36,"inner_padding_left":24,"stack_on_mobile":true}},"rows":[{"data":{"styles":{"column_layout":"1-column-full-width"}},"columns":[{"blocks":[{"content_type":"bl